<xml>
  <block type="device_stepper_driver" x="25" y="25">
    <mutation uid="motor35" />
    <field name="NAME">motor</field>
    <field name="STEP">3</field>
    <field name="DIR">4</field>
    <field name="SPEED">600</field>
    <field name="ACCEL">200</field>
    <comment pinned="false" w="340" h="170">Purpose: Describe the stepper wiring once, then control the named motor with acceleration.
Hardware: use Connections to check pin ownership for your selected board. Open the comment bubbles on the main steps for explanations.</comment>
    <field name="ENGINE">LOOP</field>
  </block>
  <block type="arduino_setup_section" x="25" y="170">
    <statement name="DO">
      <block type="device_stepper_move">
        <field name="DEVICE">motor35</field>
        <field name="MODE">TO</field>
        <value name="VALUE">
          <block type="math_number">
            <field name="NUM">800</field>
          </block>
        </value>
      </block>
    </statement>
    <comment pinned="false" w="340" h="170">Runs once after power-on or reset. Initialise the program here; repeating measurements and animation belong in loop.</comment>
  </block>
  <block type="arduino_loop_section" x="420" y="170">
    <statement name="DO">
      <block type="device_stepper_run">
        <field name="DEVICE">motor35</field>
        <next>
          <block type="controls_if">
            <value name="IF0">
              <block type="logic_compare">
                <field name="OP">EQ</field>
                <value name="A">
                  <block type="device_stepper_position">
                    <field name="DEVICE">motor35</field>
                    <field name="READ">DISTANCE</field>
                  </block>
                </value>
                <value name="B">
                  <block type="math_number">
                    <field name="NUM">0</field>
                  </block>
                </value>
              </block>
            </value>
            <statement name="DO0">
              <block type="device_stepper_move">
                <field name="DEVICE">motor35</field>
                <field name="MODE">TO</field>
                <value name="VALUE">
                  <block type="math_arithmetic">
                    <field name="OP">MINUS</field>
                    <value name="A">
                      <block type="math_number">
                        <field name="NUM">0</field>
                      </block>
                    </value>
                    <value name="B">
                      <block type="device_stepper_position">
                        <field name="DEVICE">motor35</field>
                        <field name="READ">POSITION</field>
                      </block>
                    </value>
                  </block>
                </value>
              </block>
            </statement>
            <comment pinned="false" w="340" h="170">Evaluate the condition first. Execute the enclosed actions only when it is true; otherwise skip them or use the else branch.</comment>
          </block>
        </next>
        <comment pinned="false" w="340" h="170">Service the motor on every loop pass. This emits a step only when due and returns quickly. Long delays would interrupt smooth movement.</comment>
      </block>
    </statement>
    <comment pinned="false" w="340" h="170">Repeats until power is removed. Each block runs in order, then execution returns to the top. Keep this loop responsive when servicing motors, music or serial input.</comment>
  </block>
</xml>
